## Current roadmap / platform inheritance

GitHub #78 and `docs/MESSENGER_PLATFORM_ARCHITECTURE.md` are current product/platform authority. Existing domain-specific safety rules in this file remain valid.

Current IN_APP/EMAIL delivery remains implemented. #103 adds installation-scoped push-ready destinations; future APNs/FCM arrive in #128. Push is never durable sync truth. Notification destinations use semantic NavigationTarget rather than Web href strings.


# Email notification rules

- Delivery providers sit behind replaceable adapters; auth/domain logic must not depend directly on a vendor SDK.
- Separate dev/test/prod credentials and sender identities.
- Never expose provider API keys to frontend.
- OTP/reset/security templates are localized (`ru`/`en`).
- Never include sensitive internal IDs, provider secrets or unnecessary personal data in templates.
- Reset links use short-lived single-use cryptographically strong tokens generated/managed by the auth layer.
- OTPs have bounded expiry/attempts; do not store/log raw codes unless the auth implementation requires protected temporary storage.
- Email sending has abuse controls to prevent resend spam/cost burn.
- Provider delivery failures must not leak account existence.
- Security-critical delivery events should be observable without logging message body secrets.
- Current product delivery channels are EMAIL and IN_APP. SMS is not part of the current product.
